{
  "id": "go-no-go-association-task",
  "term": "Go/No-go Association Task",
  "definition": "The Go/No-go Association Task is a social psychology task used to assess implicit attitudes by having people respond to items from selected categories while withholding responses to others. In the example described here, participants responded when a target product category and a target word type, such as positive words, appeared together, and did not respond to the other categories.",
